<title>MEXICO: Mexico silver output dips, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico silver output dips, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw output fall to 227,794 kg in October from 229,519 kg in October last year, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said Monday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production in the January-October period follows:  </p>
<p>    Product     Oct 96     Oct 95     Jan-Oct   Pct Chge Vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	   2,579	2,004	19,317	  19.4</p>
<p>    Silver     227,794    229,519   2,082.190	  -0.5</p>
<p>    Lead	  14,398     18,004     135,319	 -11.9</p>
<p>    Copper	25,404     31,025     271,372	  -3.0</p>
<p>    Zinc	  30,057     36,967     286,044	  -3.2</p>
<p>    Coal	 746,014    562,688   7,262,289	  27.2</p>
<p>    Iron	 519,808    510,422   5,142,028	  13.3</p>
<p>    Sulphur     74,597     62,609     773,423	   5.9</p>
<p>    Dolomite    78,070     81,580     768,982	   N/A</p>
<p>    Gypsum     364,687    285,447   3,074,501	   5.2</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 54,602     50,000     561,067	   N/A</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume. Figures revised from January-September figures given by INEGI.</p>
<p>Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.</p>
